<%- include('../partials/head', {
  title: 'Terms of Service',
  canonicalPath: '/terms',
  description: 'The terms that apply when RYDJA quotes and performs property work: quotes, scheduling, access, and what happens to items you authorize us to remove.'
}) %>

<main id="main" tabindex="-1" class="section shell narrow legal">
  <div class="eyebrow">TERMS OF SERVICE</div>
  <h1>Terms of Service</h1>
  <p class="lede smaller">Effective <%= termsVersion %>. These are the terms that apply when we quote and perform work for you. They are written to be read, not to be skimmed past.</p>

  <h2>Quotes</h2>
  <p>
    Sending a quote request does not create a contract, and neither does our sending you a price. Nothing is agreed
    until you approve a quote.
  </p>
  <p>
    A quote is based on what we can tell from the photos, measurements and description you give us, which means it is
    only as accurate as that information. If the actual conditions differ materially from what was described &mdash;
    substantially more volume, restricted access, items that need special handling, material we were not told about
    &mdash; we may need to revise the scope or the price before continuing. If that happens we will tell you and you
    can decide how to proceed.
  </p>

  <h2>Your authority and the property</h2>
  <p>
    By requesting work and approving a quote, you confirm that you have the authority to authorize work at the
    property and to have the items in question removed. If you are a tenant, agent, executor, contractor or anyone
    acting for someone else, that authority has to be real.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Before we remove anything, it is your responsibility to identify what must stay.</strong> We work from what
    you point out and what is on the quote. Please go through the area first and set aside or clearly mark anything you
    want to keep.
  </p>

  <h2 id="removal">Items you authorize us to remove</h2>
  <p>
    Unless we agree otherwise in writing, items you designate for removal may be disposed of, recycled, donated,
    scrapped, reused or resold at our discretion once removed. We are not able to retrieve items after they have been
    processed, and we do not hold removed items pending a change of mind.
  </p>
  <div class="panel notice">
    <h3>Please check for these before we arrive</h3>
    <p>
      Once a space is being cleared, small things are easy to lose. Please look for and remove anything of this kind
      yourself:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Identification, passports, birth certificates and immigration documents</li>
      <li>Financial records, cheque books, bank and tax paperwork</li>
      <li>Medication, medical equipment and medical records</li>
      <li>Firearms, ammunition and weapons of any kind</li>
      <li>Family photographs, letters and keepsakes</li>
      <li>Wills, deeds, titles, contracts and other legal documents</li>
      <li>Jewellery, cash, collectibles and anything with sentimental or unusual value</li>
      <li>Computers, phones, drives and anything else holding personal data</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      If you find any of these after we have started, tell the crew straight away and we will stop and set them aside.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>Hazardous and regulated material</h2>
  <p>
    You must tell us before work begins about any hazardous or regulated material you are aware of &mdash; asbestos,
    chemicals, fuels, solvents, paint, batteries, propane, biohazards, medical waste, contaminated material or
    anything similar. We are not equipped for that work and do not take it on.
  </p>
  <p>
    We may decline or stop any job that we judge to be unsafe, unlawful, beyond the scope we quoted, or outside what
    we are equipped and permitted to handle. If we stop a job for one of those reasons we will explain why.
  </p>

  <h2>Scheduling</h2>
  <p>
    An appointment time is a proposal until you confirm it. We will send you a proposed date and time; the job is not
    scheduled until you accept it on your own job page, and you can ask for a different time instead.
  </p>
  <p>
    Dates can move. Weather, equipment trouble, disposal site hours and limits, access problems at an earlier job,
    traffic, illness and emergencies all happen in this line of work. If we need to move your appointment we will
    contact you as early as we reasonably can, and we ask the same of you: if you need to cancel or reschedule, please
    let us know as early as you reasonably can.
  </p>

  <h2>Access</h2>
  <p>
    You are responsible for providing safe and lawful access to the property and to the items being removed &mdash;
    gates, keys, codes, parking, and a path the crew can actually use. If we cannot safely reach the work, we may need
    to reschedule.
  </p>

  <h2>Photographs</h2>
  <p>
    Photographs you send are used to assess the job, prepare your quote, plan the work, and document job conditions
    where that is operationally appropriate. <strong>They are not used for advertising, marketing or social media.</strong>
    If we ever want to use a photograph that way we will ask you separately and explicitly, and you are free to say no.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to these terms</h2>
  <p>
    These terms carry an effective date, and the version shown to you when you approve a quote is the version that
    applies to that job. Updating this page does not change the terms of work you have already approved.
  </p>

  <h2>Questions</h2>
  <p>
    <% if (businessPhone) { %>Call or text <a class="text-link" href="tel:<%= telHref(businessPhone) %>"><%= businessPhone %></a><% } %><% if (businessEmail) { %><% if (businessPhone) { %>, or email<% } else { %>Email<% } %> <a class="text-link" href="mailto:<%= businessEmail %>"><%= businessEmail %></a><% } %>.
    If something here is unclear, ask before you approve anything.
  </p>

  <p class="legal-foot">Last updated: October 2026 &middot; Version <%= termsVersion %></p>
</main>

<%- include('../partials/foot') %>
